    "HARAJUKU TO SHIBUYA": "原宿至澀谷",
    "These districts are close on a map but feel different on foot: Meiji Jingu opened in 1920; Harajuku was historically a post town and is now closely associated with kawaii culture; Omotesando is a broad avenue toward Aoyama; Shibuya is a major rail interchange and entertainment center. Start at the shrine and finish in Shibuya without retracing your steps.": "這幾個地區在地圖上相距不遠，實際步行時卻各有不同風貌：明治神宮於 1920 年開放；原宿昔日是宿場町，如今則與可愛文化（kawaii）密切相關；表參道是通往青山的寬闊大道；澀谷則是重要的鐵路轉乘樞紐與娛樂中心。從神宮出發，在澀谷結束行程，沿途不必走回頭路。",
    "Cat Street links Harajuku and Shibuya through smaller independent shops. Omotesando is a separate broad avenue toward Aoyama, lined with flagship stores and notable facades. Choose Cat Street for a direct area-to-area walk or Omotesando for architecture; plan the Aoyama-to-Shibuya leg separately.": "貓街串連原宿與澀谷，沿途有許多規模較小的獨立店家。表參道則是另一條通往青山的寬闊大道，沿線可見品牌旗艦店與特色建築立面。想直接從一區步行到另一區，可走貓街；若想看建築，則選表參道，並另外規劃從青山走到澀谷的路段。",
    "From the shrine, choose Takeshita for a compact fashion-and-sweets stop or quieter shrine-side streets to avoid the busiest stretch. Continue toward Shibuya on Cat Street for independent shops. Choose Omotesando for architecture and flagship stores; it leads toward Aoyama, so treat the walk back toward Shibuya as a separate leg.": "從神宮出發，可選擇逛一小段竹下通，看看時尚小店、吃些甜點；也可改走神宮旁較安靜的街道，避開最熱鬧的路段。接著沿貓街往澀谷走，逛逛獨立店家。若想欣賞建築和品牌旗艦店，可改走表參道；這條路會通往青山，因此從青山再走回澀谷時，請另行安排路線。",
    "Choose Cat Street for independent shops on the Harajuku-to-Shibuya walk. Choose Omotesando for its broad avenue and flagship architecture toward Aoyama, then plan the separate walk from Aoyama to Shibuya.": "原宿步行前往澀谷時，可選貓街逛獨立店家；若想走寬闊大道、欣賞品牌旗艦店的建築，可改走通往青山的表參道，再另外規劃從青山走到澀谷的路線。",
    "Arrive at JR Harajuku Station for Meiji Jingu or Takeshita Street, then follow the signed pedestrian route from the exit best matched to your first stop. Meiji-jingumae is useful for the south end of Omotesando or a Fukutoshin/Chiyoda Line arrival. At Shibuya, match the exit to your building; JR, Tokyu, Keio and Metro services use separate concourses.": "若要前往明治神宮或竹下通，可先抵達 JR 原宿站，再從最適合第一站的出口，依照指標步行前往。若要到表參道南端，或搭乘副都心線、千代田線抵達，明治神宮前站也很方便。抵達澀谷後，請依目的地選擇出口；JR、東急、京王與東京 Metro 的通道彼此分開。",
    "Yes. Cat Street connects Harajuku and Shibuya, with smaller independent shops along the way. Omotesando is a separate avenue toward Aoyama; include it for architecture, then plan the Aoyama-to-Shibuya leg as its own walk.": "可以。貓街連接原宿與澀谷，沿途有不少小型獨立店家。表參道則是通往青山的另一條大道；若想看建築，可以安排走表參道，再把青山至澀谷的路段當成另一段步行路線規劃。",
